Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: antacids that contain aluminum or magnesium - Gaviscon, Maalox, Milk of Magnesia, Mintox, Mylanta, Pepcid Complete, and others.
Tell your doctor about all your other medicines, especially:
orlistat;
phenobarbital, rifampin;
ketamine, steroid medicines such as dexamethasone;
antidepressants such as amitriptyline, maprotiline, or sertraline;
heart or blood pressure medication, including amiodarone, digoxin, propranolol, and other beta blockers;
furosemide given by injection;
seizure medicines such as carbamazepine or phenytoin;
high-dose aspirin, or anti-inflammatory painkillers;
estrogen, birth control pills, or tamoxifen;
testosterone or anabolic steroids;
diabetes medications, including insulin;
cancer medicine such as imatinib;
biotin or supplements that contain biotin; or
a blood thinner - warfarin, Coumadin, Jantoven.
If you have diabetes, levothyroxine can raise your blood sugar.
You may need more of your diabetes medicine or insulin.
Check your blood sugar more often when you start, change, or stop levothyroxine.
Tell your doctor about any changes.
Triplet: ["Levothyroxine", "may require adjustment of", "diabetes medicine"]

The relation 'may require adjustment of' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug may necessitate changes in the dosage or management of the medication or treatment specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has dose adjustment instruction': The subject drug may require changes in dosage based on the condition or factor specified in the object entity.
B. 'may be prescribed with': The subject drug may be prescribed in combination with the medication specified by the object entity.
C. 'may affect': The subject drug may influence or alter the physiological process or condition specified by the object entity.
D. 'used after': The subject drug is used following the treatment or condition specified by the object entity.
E. 'has recommended dose': The subject drug is typically prescribed at the dose or dosing regimen specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
